{"key":"enterprise/T1546.008","id":"T1546.008","name":"Accessibility Features","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1546","tactics":["persistence","privilege-escalation"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may establish persistence and/or elevate privileges by executing malicious content triggered by accessibility features. Windows contains accessibility features that may be launched with a key combination before a user has logged in (ex: when the user is on the Windows logon screen). An adversary can modify the way these programs are launched to get a command prompt or backdoor without logging in to the system. Two common…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1546/008","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--70e52b04-2a0c-4cea-9d18-7149f1df9dc5","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:56.964Z","source_object_version":"1.2","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0059","name":"File Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0059","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--639e87f3-acb6-448a-9645-258f20da4bc5","page":"telemetry/DC0059/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0063","name":"Windows Registry Key Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0063","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--da85d358-741a-410d-9433-20d6269a6170","page":"telemetry/DC0063/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0033","name":"Detection Strategy for Accessibility Feature Hijacking via Binary Replacement or Registry Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0033","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--05cb564b-df98-44d8-8982-176136eef26d","relationship_id":"relationship--4d6a7211-acfc-449b-bad9-8984c86cb45a"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0094","name":"Analytic 0094","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0033#AN0094","guidance":"Defenders can observe suspicious replacement or tampering of system accessibility binaries (e.g., utilman.exe, sethc.exe, osk.exe) and anomalous modifications to registry keys used to redirect accessibility programs (such as IFEO keys). Additionally, execution of cmd.exe or other suspicious binaries triggered from the login screen by SYSTEM can be correlated as part of a behavior chain.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0033"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0039","component":"File Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=11","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0094","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0033#AN0094","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0094","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0033#AN0094","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0063","component":"Windows Registry Key Modification","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=13, 14","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0094","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0033#AN0094","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0063/"},{"component_id":"DC0059","component":"File Metadata","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=15","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0094","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0033#AN0094","val